{"q":"322","t":"Coin Change","d":"Medium","p":false,"c":"<p>You are given an integer array <code>coins</code> representing coins of different denominations and an integer <code>amount</code> representing a total amount of money.</p>\n\n<p>Return <em>the fewest number of coins that you need to make up that amount</em>. If that amount of money cannot be made up by any combination of the coins, return <code>-1</code>.</p>\n\n<p>You may assume that you have an infinite number of each kind of coin.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> coins = [1,2,5], amount = 11\n<strong>Output:</strong> 3\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> 11 = 5 + 5 + 1\n</pre>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> coins = [2], amount = 3\n<strong>Output:</strong> -1\n</pre>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 3:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> coins = [1], amount = 0\n<strong>Output:</strong> 0\n</pre>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= coins.length &lt;= 12</code></li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= coins[i] &lt;= 2<sup>31</sup> - 1</code></li>\n\t<li><code>0 &lt;= amount &lt;= 10<sup>4</sup></code></li>\n</ul>\n","h":[],"m":"{\r\n  \"name\": \"coinChange\",\r\n  \"params\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"coins\",\r\n      \"type\": \"integer[]\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"amount\",\r\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"return\": {\r\n    \"type\": \"integer\"\r\n  }\r\n}","g":[{"name":"Array","slug":"array"},{"name":"Dynamic Programming","slug":"dynamic-programming"},{"name":"Breadth-First Search","slug":"breadth-first-search"},{"name":"Knapsack Problem","slug":"knapsack-problem"},{"name":"Complete Knapsack","slug":"complete-knapsack"}],"s":[{"t":"Minimum Cost For Tickets","s":"minimum-cost-for-tickets","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Maximum Value of K Coins From Piles","s":"maximum-value-of-k-coins-from-piles","d":"Hard","p":false},{"t":"Minimum Number of Operations to Convert Time","s":"minimum-number-of-operations-to-convert-time","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Minimum Cost to Split an Array","s":"minimum-cost-to-split-an-array","d":"Hard","p":false},{"t":"Count of Sub-Multisets With Bounded Sum","s":"count-of-sub-multisets-with-bounded-sum","d":"Hard","p":false},{"t":"Length of the Longest Subsequence That Sums to Target","s":"length-of-the-longest-subsequence-that-sums-to-target","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Minimum Number of Coins to be Added","s":"minimum-number-of-coins-to-be-added","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Most Expensive Item That Can Not Be Bought","s":"most-expensive-item-that-can-not-be-bought","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Inverse Coin Change","s":"inverse-coin-change","d":"Medium","p":false}],"co":[["Amazon","amazon"],["Google","google"],["Meta","facebook"],["Bloomberg","bloomberg"],["Pinterest","pinterest"],["Intuit","intuit"],["Microsoft","microsoft"],["Infosys","infosys"],["TikTok","tiktok"],["Oracle","oracle"],["Datadog","datadog"],["Accolite","accolite"],["Airbnb","airbnb"],["IBM","ibm"],["Morgan Stanley","morgan-stanley"],["C3.ai","c3-ai"],["PayPal","paypal"],["Goldman Sachs","goldman-sachs"],["Apple","apple"],["Walmart Labs","walmart-labs"],["Affirm","affirm"],["Salesforce","salesforce"],["ServiceNow","servicenow"],["Mastercard","mastercard"],["Accenture","accenture"],["PhonePe","phonepe"]],"cs":{"a":[["Google","google",11],["Amazon","amazon",9],["Meta","facebook",6],["Bloomberg","bloomberg",5],["Microsoft","microsoft",3]],"b":[["Infosys","infosys",3],["Intuit","intuit",3],["Pinterest","pinterest",3],["Grab","grab",2],["Rupeek","rupeek",2]],"m":[["Datadog","datadog",17],["TikTok","tiktok",16],["Uber","uber",10],["Goldman Sachs","goldman-sachs",8],["PayPal","paypal",8],["Oracle","oracle",7],["Walmart Labs","walmart-labs",6],["Geico","geico",5],["Fractal Analytics","fractal-analytics",5],["Apple","apple",4]]}}